os-features-api/what-data-is-available","supports_fields":["open_data_category","feature_type_open_uprn","type_name_open_uprn_address","point_geometry"]},{"accessed_at":"2026-08-01T21:40:00Z","excerpt_sha256":"2ca58e22f742312b21cddda354c803a7d500b473de5b25453398ff37525d468d","hash_scope":"normalized_official_excerpt","license_or_terms_url":"https://osdatahub.os.uk/legal/termsConditions","publisher":"Ordnance Survey","relevant_excerpt":"OS Features API accepts standard OGC XML filters. The bbox request parameter can be used for spatial selection; if bbox and a separate attribute filter are both supplied, bbox takes precedence unless they are combined inside a single OGC filter.","source_id":"os_features_filtering","source_url":"https://docs.os.uk/os-apis/accessing-os-apis/os-features-api/technical-specification/filtering","supports_fields":["ogc_filter","bbox_spatial_filter","bbox_precedence","combined_filter_rule"]},{"accessed_at":"2026-08-01T21:40:00Z","excerpt_sha256":"53f82f4db50e63fc893f9063a61ff9057b5ca6648c63e595c04182ff05d3986e","hash_scope":"normalized_official_excerpt","license_or_terms_url":"https://osdatahub.os.uk/legal/termsConditions","publisher":"Ordnance Survey","relevant_excerpt":"GetCapabilities uses the same WFS endpoint and requires the OS Data Hub API key parameter together with service WFS, request GetCapabilities and a supported WFS version.","source_id":"os_features_getcapabilities","source_url":"https://docs.os.uk/os-apis/accessing-os-apis/os-features-api/technical-specification/getcapabilities","supports_fields":["get_capabilities","key_required","service_wfs","supported_versions"]},{"accessed_at":"2026-08-01T21:40:00Z","excerpt_sha256":"6e59287cbc2f04ff883a0e4824d849ee8c6042c0514ec3e3a358e08a42608968","hash_scope":"normalized_official_excerpt","license_or_terms_url":"https://osdatahub.os.uk/legal/termsConditions","publisher":"Ordnance Survey","relevant_excerpt":"The GetFeature endpoint is https://api.os.uk/features/v1/wfs. It requires API-key or OAuth2 authentication, supports WFS 2.0.0, OpenUPRN_Address, optional bbox, count from 1 to 100 with default 100, startIndex pagination, resultType results or hits, output GML32/GML3/GML2/GEOJSON and SRS EPSG:27700/EPSG:4326/EPSG:3857.","source_id":"os_features_getfeature","source_url":"https://docs.os.uk/os-apis/accessing-os-apis/os-features-api/technical-specification/getfeature","supports_fields":["endpoint","authentication_required","open_uprn_address","bbox","count_max_100","start_index","result_type_hits","output_formats","supported_srs"]},{"accessed_at":"2026-08-01T21:40:00Z","excerpt_sha256":"93c2547a693404cbed49a070c6acbe2e4317501ca19707f3e65f1cb3c1dc915b","hash_scope":"normalized_official_excerpt","license_or_terms_url":"https://osdatahub.os.uk/legal/termsConditions","publisher":"Ordnance Survey","relevant_excerpt":"OS Features API is an OGC Web Feature Service for spatial and attribute filtering. It provides GeoJSON or XML across Great Britain, includes Open UPRN and cannot return more than 100 features in a single transaction.","source_id":"os_features_overview","source_url":"https://docs.os.uk/os-apis/accessing-os-apis/os-features-api","supports_fields":["wfs","bbox_and_attribute_filtering","geojson_xml","great_britain","max_100_features"]},{"accessed_at":"2026-08-01T21:40:00Z","excerpt_sha256":"fd4c95322feec67dbf31799619fe00e31c13a1671c1d210987277dc139777ba0","hash_scope":"normalized_official_excerpt","license_or_terms_url":"https://osdatahub.os.uk/legal/termsConditions","publisher":"Ordnance Survey","relevant_excerpt":"All OS Data Hub plan types include unlimited OpenData transactions. One OS Features API transaction is one response returning up to 100 features.","source_id":"os_plans","source_url":"https://osdatahub.os.uk/support/faqs/plans","supports_fields":["open_data_transactions_unlimited","feature_request_transaction","up_to_100_features"]},{"accessed_at":"2026-08-01T21:40:00Z","excerpt_sha256":"d8a1c24cfb319604636c52a4ca01a20020d1ddd16da